      "message": "Nit: \"they equal what `equal?` says\" holds for ilists of ilists, but not for an ipair inside an ordinary pair or vector, which the default comparator still compares with `eqv?`:\n\n- `(equal? (ilist (list (ilist 1))) (ilist (list (ilist 1))))` is #t.\n- `(\u003d? ilist-comparator (ilist (list (ilist 1))) (ilist (list (ilist 1))))` is #f.\n\nThe same holds with a vector. Maybe say \"so ilists of ilists agree with `equal?`\", and that ipairs inside other data are compared by the default comparator.",
